'' '#cmdline "-d MSG=""hello world"""' defines MSG as the STRING "hello world": the doubled
'' quotes are the literal's, the define keeps them and they group the space. fbc-modern 1.20
'' prints 'hello world 5'. tiko dropped them and read 'hello' as a name (by-example
'' BUG-preprocessor-2). See UndoubleQuotes_ / SplitCmdlineWords_ in pp/directive.tiko.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/cmdline-define-quotes.tiko -o tests/driver/cmdlinedq.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/driver/cmdlinedq.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hello world 5
